          <p>
            Note what the second row shows: the machine with the lower advertised pressure delivers roughly 30 percent more cleaning capability. If you compare only the number printed on the box, you will systematically pick the wrong machine.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-10 mb-4">How Much Pressure Each Surface Actually Wants</h3>

          <p>
            More pressure is not better. Above the level a surface tolerates, you stop cleaning and start removing the surface, and wood, paint, and mortar do not grow back. Use the widest nozzle that does the job, and step down in angle only if it does not.
